/Title (Invited to speak at the HSS Osseointegration Conference, Brian Little presented a unique case involving a 21-year-old female transfemoral amputee who underwent primary osseointegration following an elective amputation due to Complex Regional Pain Syndrome \(CRPS\). The patient had never used a socket prosthesis and also had a hip arthroplasty on the same side, leaving only 20 mm of bone between the two implants, making this a particularly complex and noteworthy case.)
